A||||5||Alex4mula||Caliper removal needed for pad change?||||1||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||10-11-2001||03:11 PM||||I have replaced many times my pads but I had always removed the calipers for one reason or other. I need to replace the pads in the front and I feel lazy today. Can it be done without removing the front calipers? Should I be able to squeeze them in? TIA<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red & White (:||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||03:26 PM||||I don't think it can be done, Sorry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||10-11-2001||04:49 PM||||On '88 Fieros it is not necessary to remove the entire caliper.<P>The '88 caliper is a 2-piece design.  You will need to remove the 2 bolts that hold the outer part to the main caliper body.  Once they are off use a large flat blade screwdriver and pop it off of the slide pins.  Now you can remove the outer pad.  You now need to remove the rotor to get to the inner pad......you may need to persuade it off, but you should get them resurfaced anyways.<P>The only way to get the pads off without removing the rotor is by completely removing the caliper from the spindle and popping off the outer half.<P><BR>Either way you do not, I repeat, do not have to remove the slide pins.  Many people (and most repair manuals) say you have to, but there is no need to ever remove these (unless they somehow got damaged).<P>Good luck......it isn't a hard job to do. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||10-11-2001||09:40 PM||||Thanks. Just ended up removing them. Took me 1.75hrs both. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||10-11-2001||10:19 PM||||I've stripped two Torx bits.<BR>Gonna hafta take it to a pro.<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000005||Standard||10-11-2001||10:51 PM||||I almost stripped one of the torx bolts on my 88, until I realized that the T-50 that works fine on my 84 and 86 fit a bit loose.. then I went out and got a T-55 bit, fit's perfect.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">         <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
